n(\lambda),
k(\lambda),
R_s(\lambda,\theta)
\}
\]

where:

- \(\sigma\) is conductivity;
- \(n\) is refractive index;
- \(k\) is the extinction coefficient;
- \(R_s\) is the measured specular response.

